#            webhook retries (0103) — a failed delivery was simply lost.
#              Deliveries now carry attempts/max_attempts/next_attempt_at and
#              climb a 1/5/30-minute ladder (initial attempt + three retries),
#              swept by a claim-based worker in the email-outbox shape so two
#              instances cannot send one event twice. `pending` means attempts
#              are still owed, `failed` means the ladder is exhausted — the
#              distinction a partner needs to tell "not yet" from "never".
#              POST /webhooks/:id/deliveries/:id/retry replays an exhausted
#              one; a delivered event cannot be replayed. This closes the
#              "specialty webhooks retry never" gap 101e309 recorded.
#
#            white-label subdomains (0106) — partners get a DNS label with a
#              reserved deny list, because a tenant holding `secure` or `login`
#              under our domain is a phishing page carrying our certificate.
#              GET /api/v1/public/branding resolves the brand from the Host
#              header, so a firm's own address renders its first frame signed
#              out without the SPA learning a slug first. It never 404s — an
#              unclaimed host is the platform and the login page has to render
#              on all of them — and host resolution is off entirely without a
#              configured base domain.
